{
  "route": "/for-providers/",
  "title": "Advertising & Provider Info | %%BRAND_NAME%%",
  "description": "Advertising options, disclosures, and how providers can request updates.",
  "main_html": "<section class=\"hero for-providers-hero\">\n  <p class=\"kicker\">Authoritative inventory</p>\n  <h1>Advertising &amp; Provider Info</h1>\n  <p class=\"muted\">Fixed inventory, contract-enforced pricing, and no pay-to-rank behavior.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section for-providers-summary\">\n  <h2>Overview</h2>\n  <p>We publish structured, location-specific industry guides and city resources designed to help users understand their options and connect with real providers serving their area.</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\">Advertising on this platform is <strong>inventory-based</strong>, <strong>disclosed</strong>, and <strong>contract-enforced</strong> \u2014 not auction-driven, not pay-to-rank, and not cluttered with uncontrolled placements.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section notice\" data-sales-page-contract=\"true\">\n  <h2>Sales page contract</h2>\n  <p class=\"muted\">This page is the authoritative inventory and pricing document. It is <strong>not</strong> an advertising surface and does not render sponsored placement blocks. Actual sponsored inventory appears only on eligible guide, city, state, and vertical-hub pages described below.</p>\n  <h3>Calls to action on live pages</h3>\n  <p>Each live page uses a three-CTA structure. These CTAs are part of the runtime page anatomy and may appear in different visual positions depending on page type, but the system is designed around three user action opportunities per page.</p>\n  <h3>How sponsor-controlled conversion works</h3>\n  <p>Sponsors do not control the educational content of the page. Sponsors control the conversion path that begins when a user enters the next-steps flow. The next-steps page is the primary conversion surface where sponsor routing, callback flow, and downstream contact logic are controlled.</p>\n  <h3>What the page-level CTAs do</h3>\n  <p>Page-level CTAs move users into the next-steps flow, request-assistance flow, or other approved action paths defined by the runtime contract. A paying sponsor does not take over the educational page itself by default; sponsor influence begins through the approved conversion surfaces that follow.</p>\n  <h3>Contract authority</h3>\n  <p>This page defines the public-facing monetization and placement contract. Runtime ad-slot behavior must match this page. Parity must be maintained by updating runtime to match the contract documented here, not by silently changing the documented sales surface after deployment.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section\">\n  <h2>Ad-slot placement by page type</h2>\n  <p class=\"muted\">These are the only placement surfaces that exist on the platform. They are fixed, validated, and enforced at build time. The /for-providers/ page itself is documentation only and never renders live sponsor blocks. If a placement would violate an active contract, the build hard-fails.</p>\n  <h3>City pages</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>top ad slot</li>\n    <li>middle ad slot</li>\n    <li>bottom ad slot</li>\n  </ul>\n  <h3>Guide pages</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>top ad slot</li>\n    <li>bottom ad slot</li>\n  </ul>\n  <h3>State pages</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>top ad slot</li>\n    <li>middle ad slot</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>No additional runtime ad placements should exist unless they are added here first.</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><strong>Hero position rule (buyouts):</strong> For Guide Buyout, City Buyout, and State Buyout, the top placement renders in a hero-style format rather than creating a new slot.</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><strong>Shared placements:</strong> Shared placements are stacked and we do not state a hard cap on the number of shared sponsors.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section for-providers-commercial\">\n  <h2>Sponsorship tiers <span class=\"h2-sub\">(monthly pricing + scope)</span></h2>\n\n  <div class=\"tiers\">\n\n\n    <div class=\"tier\">\n      <h3>City \u2014 Shared Placement (Stacked) <span class=\"price\">$2,500 / city</span></h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li>City page: Top placement + Middle + Bottom (3 placements)</li>\n        <li>Shared (stacked): multiple sponsors may appear in these positions</li>\n</ul>\n      <div class=\"actions\">\n        <a class=\"btn primary\" href=\"mailto:info@spryvc.com?subject=Sponsorship%20Inquiry%20%E2%80%94%20City%20Shared%20Placement%20%28Stacked%29&body=Full%20name%3A%0AWork%20email%3A%0APhone%3A%0AFirm%20name%3A%0AFirm%20type%3A%0AInterested%20in%3A%20City%20Shared%20Placement%20%28Stacked%29%0APrimary%20markets%3A%0AEstimated%20monthly%20budget%3A%0AHow%20did%20you%20find%20us%3A%0A\">Sponsorship inquiry</a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"tier\">\n      <h3>City \u2014 Buyout (Exclusive) <span class=\"price\">$5,000 / city</span></h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li>City page: Top placement + Middle + Bottom (3 placements)</li>\n        <li>Exclusive: only your brand appears in these positions (subject to contract hierarchy rules)</li>\n        <li>Top placement renders hero-style</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"actions\">\n        <a class=\"btn primary\" href=\"mailto:info@spryvc.com?subject=Sponsorship%20Inquiry%20%E2%80%94%20City%20Buyout%20%28Exclusive%29&body=Full%20name%3A%0AWork%20email%3A%0APhone%3A%0AFirm%20name%3A%0AFirm%20type%3A%0AInterested%20in%3A%20City%20Buyout%20%28Exclusive%29%0APrimary%20markets%3A%0AEstimated%20monthly%20budget%3A%0AHow%20did%20you%20find%20us%3A%0A\">Sponsorship inquiry</a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"tier\">\n      <h3>State Buyout (PI only) <span class=\"price\">$30,000 / state</span></h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li>State hub: Top (hero position) + Middle (2 placements)</li>\n        <li>Cumulative coverage across all covered city pages in the state</li>\n        <li><strong>Expansion right:</strong> You have the right to add additional cities within the same state <strong>upon request</strong> as we expand coverage (most states begin with at least two major metro areas). Added cities become part of the state buyout coverage under the same state contract, subject to hierarchy/conflict rules.</li>\n        <li>Top placement renders hero-style</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"actions\">\n        <a class=\"btn primary\" href=\"mailto:info@spryvc.com?subject=Sponsorship%20Inquiry%20%E2%80%94%20State%20Buyout%20%28PI%20Only%29&body=Full%20name%3A%0AWork%20email%3A%0APhone%3A%0AFirm%20name%3A%0AFirm%20type%3A%0AInterested%20in%3A%20State%20Buyout%20%28PI%20Only%29%0APrimary%20markets%3A%0AEstimated%20monthly%20budget%3A%0AHow%20did%20you%20find%20us%3A%0A\">Sponsorship inquiry</a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"tier\">\n      <h3>Vertical Pack (total website) Buyout <span class=\"price\">$75,000</span></h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Includes vertical hub hero, plus eligible pages across the vertical (subject to contract hierarchy rules)</li>\n        <li>Enables the Vertical Buyout runtime \u201cNext Steps\u201d CTA on eligible pages (below)</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"actions\">\n        <a class=\"btn primary\" href=\"mailto:info@spryvc.com?subject=Sponsorship%20Inquiry%20%E2%80%94%20Vertical%20Pack%20Buyout&body=Full%20name%3A%0AWork%20email%3A%0APhone%3A%0AFirm%20name%3A%0AFirm%20type%3A%0AInterested%20in%3A%20Vertical%20Pack%20Buyout%0APrimary%20markets%3A%0AEstimated%20monthly%20budget%3A%0AHow%20did%20you%20find%20us%3A%0A\">Sponsorship inquiry</a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section for-providers-mechanics\">\n  <h2>What slots look like (visual)</h2>\n  <p class=\"muted\">These visuals represent real inventory surfaces. Sponsors are <strong>stacked</strong> within a placement (static), not side-by-side, and not rotating.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"visuals-list\">\n\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section\">\n  <h2>Vertical Buyout Runtime \u201cNext Steps\u201d Mechanism</h2>\n  <p class=\"muted\">When a vertical buyout is active, eligible pages display a runtime \u201cNext Steps\u201d CTA. Locked CTA copy: \u201cReview the local next-step guide before choosing a provider.\u201d</p>\n  <p class=\"muted\"><strong>Locked CTA copy (vertical buyout only):</strong> Review the local next-step guide before choosing a provider.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"visuals-list\">\n    \n    <details class=\"visual-card accordion\">\n      <summary>Runtime on a Guide Page (CTA appears)</summary>\n      <div class=\"svg-wrap\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1300\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 1300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Runtime on a Guide Page: Next Steps CTA appears when vertical buyout is active.\">\n  <defs>\n    <style>\n      .bg{fill:#f6f7fb}\n      .frame{fill:#ffffff;stroke:#e6e8f0;stroke-width:2}\n      .topbar{fill:#0b1220}\n      .topbarText{fill:#ffffff;font:700 18px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .title{fill:#0f172a;font:900 28px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .sub{fill:#475569;font:500 16px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .ctaWrap{fill:#0b1220}\n      .ctaText{fill:#ffffff;font:900 18px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .ctaSub{fill:#cbd5e1;font:600 13px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .btn{fill:#ffffff;stroke:#cbd5e1;stroke-width:2}\n      .btnText{fill:#0f172a;font:900 14px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .pill{fill:#f59e0b}\n      .pillText{fill:#0b1220;font:900 12px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n      .content{fill:#f1f5fb;stroke:#e6e8f0;stroke-width:2}\n      .line{fill:#e8edf6}\n      .sectionHdr{fill:#0f172a;font:800 15px Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif}\n    </style>\n  </defs>\n  <rect class=\"bg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1300\"/>\n  <rect class=\"frame\" x=\"80\" y=\"60\" width=\"1040\" height=\"1180\" rx=\"18\"/>\n  <rect class=\"topbar\" x=\"80\" y=\"60\" width=\"1040\" height=\"54\" rx=\"18\"/>\n  <text class=\"topbarText\" x=\"110\" y=\"95\">Guide Page</text>\n  <text class=\"topbarText\" x=\"1010\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"end\">Runtime CTA</text>\n  <text class=\"title\" x=\"120\" y=\"155\">Runtime on a Guide Page (CTA appears)</text>\n  <text class=\"sub\" x=\"120\" y=\"185\">When a vertical buyout is active, eligible pages display a runtime CTA.</text>\n  <rect class=\"ctaWrap\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\" width=\"960\" height=\"120\" rx=\"16\"/>\n  <rect class=\"pill\" x=\"150\" y=\"245\" width=\"158\" height=\"28\" rx=\"999\"/>\n  <text class=\"pillText\" x=\"229\" y=\"264\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NEXT STEPS</text>\n  <text class=\"ctaText\" x=\"150\" y=\"298\">Review the local next-step guide before choosing a provider.</text>\n  <text class=\"ctaSub\" x=\"150\" y=\"322\">Vertical buyout active \u2022 runtime CTA appears on this guide page</text>\n  <rect class=\"btn\" x=\"830\" y=\"265\" width=\"210\" height=\"52\" rx=\"12\"/>\n  <text class=\"btnText\" x=\"935\" y=\"297\" text-anchor=\"middle\">View next steps</text>\n  <text class=\"sectionHdr\" x=\"120\" y=\"385\">Editorial content</text>\n  <rect class=\"content\" x=\"120\" y=\"403\" width=\"960\" height=\"360\" rx=\"16\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"460\" width=\"820\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"490\" width=\"760\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"520\" width=\"840\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"550\" width=\"720\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"580\" width=\"800\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"610\" width=\"760\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"content\" x=\"120\" y=\"785\" width=\"960\" height=\"230\" rx=\"16\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"845\" width=\"780\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <rect class=\"line\" x=\"160\" y=\"875\" width=\"720\" h